# Copy to C:\ProgramData\KidTablet\.env to let Draw With Me learn drawings it does not have.
# Without this file, Draw With Me uses its built-in drawings and library.js only.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# Optional:
# DRAW_DAILY_LIMIT=25
# DRAW_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5-5

# Story Maker (optional). Stories are written live by Claude with the key above; without it a built-in story is used.
# STORY_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5-20251001
# Live voices, one per character. Without any of these, Windows voices are used.
# voicestudio: the VoiceStudio app on your PC with the designed cast in apps/story-maker/voices.js. The desktop app
# binds to localhost only, so on the PC put in %USERPROFILE%\.config\omnivoice\env:
#   OMNIVOICE_API_KEY=<long random key>            admin routes need it from anywhere but the PC
#   OMNIVOICE_TRUSTED_NETWORKS=10.0.0.0/24          the tablet's subnet may use the voices with no credential
#   OMNIVOICE_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=null,http://localhost:3901,http://127.0.0.1:3901,tauri://localhost,http://tauri.localhost,app://voicestudio
# and set the user variable OMNIVOICE_BACKEND_CMD to the app's backend command with --host 0.0.0.0 (see README), then
# restart VoiceStudio. Leave TTS_PIN unset with a trusted subnet; set it to the share PIN (port 3901, Settings > Sharing)
# or OMNIVOICE_API_KEY otherwise. Works at home only; an Azure or OpenAI key below is used when the PC cannot be reached.
# TTS_PROVIDER=voicestudio
# TTS_URL=http://10.0.0.169:3900
# TTS_PIN=
# Azure Speech (region + key) or OpenAI (key only). Primary when TTS_PROVIDER=azure|openai, fallback with voicestudio.
# TTS_FALLBACK=azure
# TTS_REGION=eastus
# TTS_KEY=...
